Draft a bilingual job description (English + native Gulf Arabic) from the role
spec below. Every field here is a signal candidates use to self-filter — reflect
each one somewhere in the JD. Do NOT invent facts beyond what the spec implies.

ROLE SPEC
=========

Title:           {{ title }}
Hiring company:  {{ hiring_company }}
Location:        {{ city }}, {{ country_display }}
Employment type: {{ employment_type }}
Work mode:       {{ work_mode }}
Compensation:    {{ compensation }}
Notice period:   {{ notice_period or '(not specified)' }}
Min experience:  {{ min_experience_years }} year(s)
Visa stance:     {{ visa_requirement or 'Open to all visas' }}
Nationality:     {{ nationality_preference | join(', ') if nationality_preference else 'Any nationality' }}
Languages req'd: {{ languages_required | join(', ') if languages_required else '(none specified)' }}

Required skills:  {{ required_skills | join(', ') if required_skills else '(none listed)' }}
Preferred skills: {{ preferred_skills | join(', ') if preferred_skills else '(none listed)' }}

INSTRUCTIONS
============
- Lead the requirements with the {{ min_experience_years }}+ years of experience
  and the Required skills; weave in the Preferred skills as "nice to have".
- Include the salary ONLY if the Compensation line above gives a real band —
  if it reads "(not specified)", omit salary entirely (never "competitive salary").
- Write for a {{ city }}, {{ country_display }} hiring market.
- The Arabic rendering must be written natively, not translated from the English.
- Return both renderings via the structured output tool (job_description_en,
  job_description_ar).
